## 1. Purpose and principles

This document keeps {{tool_name}} in a validated state after release. It works as a predetermined change protocol for the tool: it states in advance which future changes are pre-authorised and the exact tests that authorise them, so that routine changes (above all new models) need a defined test subset, not a new validation.

- **Configuration** (settings, rules, hooks, MCP servers, instruction files, code-host gates, model envelope) is baselined in {{doc_id_06}} and changes only through a change record.
- **Behaviour** varies: models change, sometimes without a version change. It is covered by the vendor monitoring routine (section 5), the model admission check MA-01 and the periodic review (section 6).
- Three tiers:
  1. **Initial validation** (once per tool and vendor): full IQ / OQ / PQ of the guardrails plus MA-01 on every model in the initial envelope ({{doc_id_05}}, {{doc_id_07}}).
  2. **Model admission** (MA-01 only, per new model or model version that matches a pre-authorised pattern of {{doc_id_04}} section 5.2): pass, and the model joins the envelope with an admission record (section 7), which is the revalidation record permitted by the software validation procedure cited in {{doc_id_04}} section 2.
  3. **Re-baseline** (on the triggers in section 4): a defined confirmatory subset of tests.
- Tests that change for a trigger are chosen from {{doc_id_05}}; their acceptance criteria do not change. A criterion may change only through a revision of {{doc_id_05}} approved before the re-test.

Regulatory anchors:
{{#reg_iso13485}}
- ISO 13485:2016 clause 4.1.6: validation after changes to the software or its application, proportionate to risk; clause 7.4: supplier monitoring and re-evaluation.
{{/reg_iso13485}}
{{#reg_fda_qmsr}}
- 21 CFR Part 820 (QMSR), incorporating ISO 13485:2016 by reference; FDA CSA guidance (risk-based assurance, including for software changes). 21 CFR Part 11 applies to the records of this package that are kept or signed electronically.
{{/reg_fda_qmsr}}
{{#reg_gxp}}
- EU GMP Annex 11 clauses 10 (change and configuration management) and 11 (periodic evaluation).
{{/reg_gxp}}
- ISO/TR 80002-2:2017, Maintain phase: keep the validated state while managing changes; monitoring of use or configuration can be appropriate because both can drift, and a change of intended use can require more validation even without a software change.

## 2. Model policy for this tool

Model policy: **{{model_policy}}**.

{{#policy_envelope}}
Envelope policy: the output is independently verified downstream (human review and CI), so any admitted model inside the envelope may be used. A new model id that matches a pre-authorised pattern ({{doc_id_04}} section 5.2) and meets the eligibility rows of section 7 is admitted with MA-01 only; any other new id is T3. The enforced allow-list holds admitted ids only. The model used is recorded per PR / session.
{{/policy_envelope}}
{{#policy_pinned}}
Pinned policy: the AI output itself counts as a control or as evidence, so only the exact model `{{pinned_model}}` may be used. Any model change (including a new version of the same model) needs the confirmatory subset CS-2 and an approved change record before use.
{{/policy_pinned}}

